    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261">

                <pb facs="0446" n="352" xml:id="pg352"/>

                <head>No. 261.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. McLane</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 8,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 270.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to recent correspondence in the
                    case of Baron Raymond Seillière, I inclose for your information copies of
                    certain papers filed in the Department by Mr. Bullock, of California, and of
                    correspondence with Messrs. Develin and Miller, of New York, all relating to the
                    request that the Department should certify to Baron Seillière’s domicile.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. BAYARD.</hi></signed></closer>







